From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:06:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 901/913] drivers: stm32_uart: fix baudrate parsing and
 prescaler index check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Coverity reports two defects in stm32_uart_update_baudrate():

- CERT ERR30-C: the return value of strtoul() is used without any
  check. When the device tree parameter is not a valid number, or is
  zero, baudrate is 0 and the UDIV_ROUND_NEAREST() computation ends up
  dividing by zero. Reject a null baudrate before entering the loop.

- ARR30-C/OVERRUN on presc[i]: the loop exits either with the break
  statement or with the in-loop test on the last index, so index
  ARRAY_SIZE(presc) is never reached. The analyser cannot correlate
  both exit conditions and reports an out-of-bounds read. Drop the
  redundant in-loop test and check the loop index once the loop has
  completed, which makes the bound explicit.

No functional change in nominal cases.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 65595f6570e0304ab1156413729c04427d1a5eca drivers: stm32_uart: fix baudrate parsing and prescaler index check]
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Change-Id: I0fd2d059ccc951918de79ed7c317b5c804cb4c96
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/613440
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_uart.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c b/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c
index 05d824bf0..c884bc0fa 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c
@@ -165,6 +165,8 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_uart_update_baudrate(struct stm32_uart_pdata *pd,
 		panic();
 
 	baudrate = strtoul(params, NULL, 10);
+	if (!baudrate)
+		return TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(presc); i++) {
 		uartdiv = UDIV_ROUND_NEAREST(clk_rate, baudrate * presc[i]);
@@ -180,9 +182,11 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_uart_update_baudrate(struct stm32_uart_pdata *pd,
 
 		if (brr <= UART_REG_BRR_MASK)
 			break;
-		if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(presc) - 1)
-			return TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
 	}
+
+	if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(presc))
+		return TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
+
 	io_write32(uart_base + UART_REG_BRR, brr);
 	io_write32(uart_base + UART_REG_PRESC, presc[i]);
 	io_write32(uart_base + UART_REG_CR1, UART_REG_CR1_UE |
